  "name": "CMOS Bandgap Voltage Reference",
  "description": "Classic Brokaw-style bandgap reference implemented in CMOS using parasitic PNP bipolar transistors (substrate BJTs available in SKY130). Combines a PTAT (Proportional to Absolute Temperature) voltage from the ΔVbe path with the negative temperature coefficient of Vbe to produce a temperature-stable ~1.2V reference voltage.",
  "category": "Analog",
  "technology": ["SKY130"],
  "keywords": ["bandgap", "bandgap reference", "voltage reference", "vref", "temperature stable reference", "brokaw", "bgr"],
